#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A mixed catalog for the desk: thirty entries made out of the three
published apps' assets, so the interactive emulator shows a list that has a
bit of everything -- every tab's tag, an app in two tabs and one in All
alone, two plugins, names short enough to fit and one
long enough to be clipped, entries missing an icon, a screenshot, a film or
all three, summaries of every length, three authors, and a third of the rows
in each install state.

Called by dev/start --mock; not meant to be run by hand.

    mock-catalog make  --work DIR --ms DIR [--url URL]
    mock-catalog clean --work DIR --ms DIR

make writes the site under <work>/mock-site, plants db records and PSP/GAME
directories on the emulator's stick, and lists everything it planted in
<work>/mock-planted. It also names the mock catalog alone in the stick's
PSP/PSPDX/sources.txt, keeping the user's sources.txt and presets.seen
beside them as <name>.mock-backup (or a <name>.mock-absent mark when there
was none). clean removes the planted things, and anything else on the stick
wearing the mock's id or directory prefix, and nothing besides: the user's
own installs live in the same directories and carry neither prefix. It puts
the two files back as they were, byte for byte, or takes the mock's away
where there was none; run twice, the second run finds nothing to do.

The generation is seeded and the assets are cached, so the same list comes
back every time and only the first run goes to the network.
"""
import hashlib, io, json, os, random, shutil, sys, time, urllib.request, zipfile

